{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Go for peer upgrade, ledger refactoring, and LCCC sanity-check code (consistent with Hyperledger Fabric v1.0 implementation language).",
    "Use Node.js / TypeScript for the Fabric Node SDK to align with existing SDK ecosystem conventions.",
    "Adopt Markdown (and AsciiDoc where the repo already uses it) for documentation deliverables, generated/stored alongside the source code.",
    "Implement peer upgrade via the existing Lifecycle Chaincode (LCCC) and System Chaincode (SCC) abstractions rather than introducing a new mechanism.",
    "Treat U4 (ledger refactor) as a purely internal cleanup: replace remaining old block-structure references with the new Block/BlockHeader structures introduced earlier, and inject an MSP interface in tests instead of importing concrete MSP security packages.",
    "For U7, add an input validation guard (allowlist) in the chaincode invocation dispatch path so only LCCC and user-deployed chaincodes can be invoked.",
    "For U5/U6 documentation, rely on Sphinx-generated docs plus lightweight scripts (bash/Go) and a small set of architecture diagrams drawn in an existing tool already used by the project.",
    "Provide a thin compatibility shim in the Node SDK for chaincode invocation and channel-related queries so that the SDK tracks the Go API surface being added under FAB-687."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One workday equals 8 hours; the developer is already familiar with the Hyperledger Fabric v1.0 codebase, so no ramp-up beyond a brief re-orientation is needed.",
    "A development environment (Go toolchain, Node.js, Fabric test network scripts, Docker, git, gerrit workflow) is already available and does not need to be set up from scratch.",
    "External dependencies (e.g., the patch series linked from U2, the LCCC implementation referenced by U3/U7) are either already merged or will be provided by other contributors; this increment integrates with them rather than implementing them from zero.",
    "U5 visual aids are limited to static architecture diagrams and runnable demo scripts (no interactive demos, slides, or video production).",
    "The Node SDK (U8) targets the same set of capabilities as the existing Go SDK at the v1.0 sprint-6 baseline: identity/MSP, channel creation, chaincode lifecycle, and basic query/invoke.",
    "Effort estimates include design, implementation, unit tests, and local integration testing; they do not include multi-party system testing, performance benchmarking, or release management.",
    "No code-review back-and-forth cycles beyond a single round of fixes are included; large redesigns are out of scope."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Codebase re-orientation and environment check",
      "activity_description": "Refresh understanding of the Fabric v1.0 peer, ledger, chaincode shim, and SDK directories; verify build, test, and lint scripts run end-to-end before changes begin.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Getting-started / visitor landing documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write a concise 'Getting Started' page aimed at first-time visitors: what Fabric is, where to find samples, how to read the docs, and pointers to v0.6 vs v1.0.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - New-channel configuration transaction documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the structure of the new-channel configuration transaction produced by the FAB-687 API: fields, allowed values, defaults, and example payloads; cross-link to the gerrit change referenced in the story.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Peer upgrade mechanism (LCCC + SCC)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the in-place peer upgrade path so that protocol changes can be applied without data loss: wire up the Lifecycle Chaincode for chaincode upgrades and the System Chaincode path for patches/fixes unrelated to protocol changes, including basic state migration hooks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Ledger code cleanup (remove old block structure)",
      "activity_description": "Audit the ledger package and replace remaining usages of the old block structure with the new Block/BlockHeader types; ensure all construction paths use the up-to-date types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Ledger test cleanup and MSP decoupling",
      "activity_description": "Update ledger unit tests to use the new block structure and remove the explicit dependency on MSP security packages by injecting identities/principals through an interface or test stub.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Architecture documentation, diagrams, and demo scripts",
      "activity_description": "Produce an architecture overview document and a small set of diagrams (peers, orderers, channels, chaincode flow) and accompanying scripts that can be executed to demonstrate Fabric v1.0 behavior as of the end of sprint 6.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U6 - v1.0 / v0.6 documentation guidance",
      "activity_description": "Update doc index, READMEs, and topic pages so that users seeking a stable operational platform are directed to v0.6, while v1.0 docs cover the in-development usage model and known limitations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U7 - LCCC and chaincode invocation sanity check",
      "activity_description": "Add an allowlist-style validation in the chaincode invocation path so that only LCCC and user-deployed (normal) chaincodes can be invoked; reject any other names with a clear error, and cover with unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Fabric Node SDK implementation",
      "activity_description": "Develop a Node.js SDK exposing: identity/MSP enrollment, channel creation (consuming the new-channel config from U2), chaincode install/instantiate/upgrade, and query/invoke. Include a thin client, error types, and unit tests mirroring key Go SDK coverage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration testing across peer, ledger, and Node SDK",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end scenarios combining the upgraded peer (A4), refactored ledger (A5/A6), and the new Node SDK (A10) against a local test network; fix issues uncovered by the integration runs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Code review rework, bug fixes, and polish",
      "activity_description": "Address a single round of review comments across all change sets, fix minor defects found during integration, and finalize documentation cross-links.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 48
  }
}
```

